# Big Fat Dark Chocolate Cranberry Oatmeal Cookies

Based on [Sally’s Baking Addiction](https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/dark-chocolate-cranberry-oatmeal-cookies)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 cup (2 sticks; 226g) [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, softened
- [ ] 1 cup (200g) [packed light]{ ing="packed-light" } or dark brown sugar
- [ ] 1/2 cup (100g) [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] 2 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, room temperature
- [ ] 1 Tbsp (21g) [unsulphured or dark molasses]{ ing="unsulphured-or-dark-molasses" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [pure vanilla extract]{ ing="pure-vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 2 cups (170g) [old-fashioned whole rolled oats]{ ing="old-fashioned-whole-rolled-oats" }
- [ ] 1.5 cups (188g) [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }
- [ ] 1 cup (118g) [cake flour]{ ing="cake-flour" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }
- [ ] 3/4 tsp [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [ground cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 6 ounces (170g) [chopped bittersweet]{ ing="chopped-bittersweet" } or dark chocolate
- [ ] 1 cup (150g) [dried cranberries]{ ing="dried-cranberries" }
- [ ] 3/4 cup (90g) [chopped walnuts]{ ing="chopped-walnuts" }

## Recipe

1. Whisk together [oats]{ ing="old-fashioned-whole-rolled-oats" }, [flours]{ ing="cake-flour" }, [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }, [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }, [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }, [cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" } in a large bowl. Set aside
1. Beat [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" } and both [sugars]{ ing="granulated-sugar" } on medium-high speed until creamy (about 3 minutes). Add [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, [molasses]{ ing="unsulphured-or-dark-molasses" }, and vanilla. Beat until combined
1. Add dry mixture, chocolate, [cranberries]{ ing="dried-cranberries" }, and [walnuts]{ ing="chopped-walnuts" } to wet ingredients. Mix on low speed until combined
1. Cover and refrigerate dough for at least 1 hour (up to 4 days)
1. Preheat oven to 400F. Line baking sheets with parchment paper
1. Scoop dough using a 1/3-cup measure. Place 5-6 cookies per sheet
1. Bake 5 minutes, then reduce temperature to 350F and bake 10 additional minutes
1. Cool on baking sheet for 10-20 minutes before transferring to wire rack

## Notes

- Cookies remain fresh, covered at room temperature, for up to one week
- Also see the main cookie recipe: [Chocolate Chip Cookies](./chocolate_chip_cookies.html)
- Other oatmeal cookie variations: [Chocolate Chip Oatmeal Cookies](./chocolate_chip_oatmeal_cookies.html), [Soft & Chewy Oatmeal Raisin Cookies](./soft_chewy_oatmeal_raisin_cookies.html)
